{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TtUMNLiCo3wDwQvk4NAd3g","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, I found the answer:\\\\n\\\\nWhen the `--cluster-id` flag is used with the storage formatting tool, the formatter writes **meta.properties V2**.\\\\n\\\\nThis is documented in Jun Rao's feedback on KIP-1262 (Enable auto-formatting directories), where he specifically noted:\\\\n\\\\n> **JR11: Prefers V2 format over V1 for new cluster-id writes**\\\\n\\\\nThe rationale for using V2 is that MetaProperties V2 allows `cluster.id` to be optional, whereas V1 requires it. When the `--cluster-id` flag is explicitly provided during formatting, V2 is the appropriate format to write.\\\\n\\\\n**Files cited:**\\\\n- `/store/discussions.md` (line 304, in the Window 78 KIP-1262 discussion)\\\\n- `/store/pull-requests.md` (line 7847, PR #21547 describing MetaProperties V2 semantics)\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"index.md\\\",\\\"discussions.md\\\",\\\"pull-requests.md\\\",\\\"issues.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":72.67,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":3,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":1006028,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":54647,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.2302708,\\\"input_tokens\\\":194,\\\"output_tokens\\\":4036}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e7c64dfd-3f70-45f6-b9c5-86fd1b0b0b98","uuid":"ef03be9f-2af6-4135-b157-5cd0a168e75c","timestamp":"2026-09-27T18:23:26.992Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, I found the answer:\\\\n\\\\nWhen the `--cluster-id` flag is used with the storage formatting tool, the formatter writes **meta.properties V2**.\\\\n\\\\nThis is documented in Jun Rao's feedback on KIP-1262 (Enable auto-formatting directories), where he specifically noted:\\\\n\\\\n> **JR11: Prefers V2 format over V1 for new cluster-id writes**\\\\n\\\\nThe rationale for using V2 is that MetaProperties V2 allows `cluster.id` to be optional, whereas V1 requires it. When the `--cluster-id` flag is explicitly provided during formatting, V2 is the appropriate format to write.\\\\n\\\\n**Files cited:**\\\\n- `/store/discussions.md` (line 304, in the Window 78 KIP-1262 discussion)\\\\n- `/store/pull-requests.md` (line 7847, PR #21547 describing MetaProperties V2 semantics)\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"index.md\\\",\\\"discussions.md\\\",\\\"pull-requests.md\\\",\\\"issues.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":72.67,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":3,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":1006028,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":54647,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.2302708,\\\"input_tokens\\\":194,\\\"output_tokens\\\":4036}}\"}","_meta":{"fastmcp":{"wrap_result":true}},"structuredContent":{"result":"{\"answer\":\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, I found the answer:\\n\\nWhen the `--cluster-id` flag is used with the storage formatting tool, the formatter writes **meta.properties V2**.\\n\\nThis is documented in Jun Rao's feedback on KIP-1262 (Enable auto-formatting directories), where he specifically noted:\\n\\n> **JR11: Prefers V2 format over V1 for new cluster-id writes**\\n\\nThe rationale for using V2 is that MetaProperties V2 allows `cluster.id` to be optional, whereas V1 requires it. When the `--cluster-id` flag is explicitly provided during formatting, V2 is the appropriate format to write.\\n\\n**Files cited:**\\n- `/store/discussions.md` (line 304, in the Window 78 KIP-1262 discussion)\\n- `/store/pull-requests.md` (line 7847, PR #21547 describing MetaProperties V2 semantics)\",\"error\":null,\"files\":[\"index.md\",\"discussions.md\",\"pull-requests.md\",\"issues.md\"],\"seconds\":72.67,\"truncated\":false,\"turns\":3,\"usage\":{\"cache_read_tokens\":1006028,\"cache_write_tokens\":54647,\"cost_usd\":0.2302708,\"input_tokens\":194,\"output_tokens\":4036}}"}}}
